==English==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|toe|rag|lang=en}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[rag]] worn around the foot in place of a [[sock]].
#*'''1989''', {{w|Keith Bosley}}, translating Elias Lönnrot, ''The Kalevala'', XLIV:
#*:Steady old Väinämöinen / yonder crept with no shoes on / without '''toe-rags''' he tiptoed […].
# A [[tramp]] or [[vagrant]].
# A [[worthless]] or despicable person.
#* '''2007''', {{w|J. K. Rowling}}, ''Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows'', USA: Arthur A. Levine Books (2007), page 674:
#*:"I know James Potter's an arrogant '''toerag'''," she said, cutting across Snape.

